From 036825275f5fed4521a60a083ae65f919a47a732 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viktor Semenov <suit.uanic@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 09:40:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] Resume a replay from a dumped state and report its result
 on dump runs

-replay-initial-state=PATH loads a state written by -dump-state-out once
the game has started, where a rejoining client loads it, and continues from
the wire turn it was dumped at. The replay file then carries only the turns
after it, so the dedicated server can chain short runs instead of replaying
a whole match from turn 0 every time.

Loading happens after ReallyStartGame on purpose: InitGame runs there and
resets the statistics history of any state loaded before it.

A file that is missing, truncated or does not deserialize, or a replay file
whose first block does not continue from the loaded turn, logs why and
exits 1 instead of hitting an ENSURE, which in a headless process can wait
on stdin or fork a debugger.

A dump run now also prints REPLAY_RESULT, so one run yields both the state
and the match so far.
